cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Good Practices in R
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, or reuse, adapt, or
  expand on its content in your own training material.
authors:
  - name: Good Practices in R contributors
    website: https://github.com/UCL-ARC/r-intermediate-good-practices/graphs/contributors
abstract: >-
  An intermediate R lesson on writing reproducible and maintainable
  research software. The current material introduces reproducible
  workflows and project dependency management with renv. Draft
  episodes cover testing, code smells, refactoring, documentation,
  packaging, and reproducibility.
keywords:
  - R
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - good practices
url: https://github.com/UCL-ARC/r-intermediate-good-practices
repository-code: https://github.com/UCL-ARC/r-intermediate-good-practices
license: CC-BY-4.0
